 報名/票券: https://digitaleconomy.stanford.edu/event/richard-socher-de
 l-seminar-series/\n\nThe next\, maybe final\, frontier of AI research is a
 utomating the process of knowledge discovery. By pointing AI first at itse
 lf and then at the R&D process of all scientific domains\, we can far exce
 ed where human-led research can take us. Richard Socher argues the current
  pace of scientific discovery has slowed significantly over the past sever
 al decades as the fields of science fragment and the number of researchers
  focused on any one continues to shrink.\n\nThe answer to this generationa
 l challenge is to automate the scientific method itself. He will lay out t
 he architecture of a full-stack scientific superintelligence: a living map
  of human knowledge\, a unified model of physical reality\, high-fidelity 
 simulation\, autonomous laboratories\, and an agent swarm that works the w
 ay a scientific community does. He will explain why recursive self-improve
 ment is how you build it and why the first science to automate is the scie
 nce of AI itself\, and share early results from Recursive\, the new compan
 y he co-founded to build it.
